|name2 = Ballistic Dragon Gunduros
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Ballistic Dragon Gunduros''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Gunduros is a very promising nuker, boasting 500 standing range which lets it stand away safely from most common enemies within its targets. It has a high 70K base DPH at Lv.30, which jumps to 282,200 effective DPH, or 19.6K DPS, against Dark/Alien with its [[Massive Damage]] assuming maxed [[Fruit Treasures]]. This damage is high enough to almost instantly vaporize most weaker targets like [[Star Peng]] and [[Shadow Boxer K]] at standard magnification, while severely crippling others. Gunduros also sports a good amount of bulk, with 119K health and two knockbacks to give it a great chance at attacking anything that might be close to it, provided it manages to get an attack out in the first place before anything happens to it.

Gunduros' most notable catch is its unforgivingly long attack cycle of around 14.4 seconds, made more inconvenient by its foreswing of 7.4 seconds. Gunduros is likely to miss attacks entirely if the frontline pushes or gets pushed even slightly, lacking piercing range via Long Distance or Omni Strike. While Aliens tend to hold most of their power in their status effects, thus being nullified by proper counterplay, Dark enemies specialize in speed and immense damage output. While most of them don't outrange Gunduros, their aggressive pushing power and high knockback count means that it will prove harder for Gunduros to get an attack off before they either beat Gunduros into scrap metal or get knocked outside of its attacking range. If Gunduros goes down, it will be a long while before another one comes out, due to its over 2 minute cooldown and luxurious price tag of 5,925.

If Gunduros manages to hit its target traits, however, Dark/Alien enemies will be [[Knockback|knocked back]] (assuming the sheer damage isn't already enough to stagger them) and [[Slow|Slowed down]] for 8 whole seconds, providing some time for Gunduros to safely recharge its next devastating attack. You can optimize the amount of time enemies spend away from Gunduros or help it land hits with its [[Conjure]], [[Freeze|Freezing]] any enemy it hits for 3.33 seconds. Gunduros' Conjure can also help give breathing room for your units in general, allowing them to land additional hits or live longer. However, as with other Conjures, it's a one-time ability, so do your best to make the most of it and try not to use it recklessly so as to not cause Gunduros to miss an attack. This also means that Gunduros cannot be stacked, unlike most nukers.

Gunduros is also [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immune]], which can help it face off against enemies like [[Two Can]]/[[Youcan]], [[Bun Bun Symbiote]], and [[Dark Dober]], with the last matchup also being majorly improved by Gunduros' [[Sage Slayer]] ability. With this, Gunduros has an additional niche, being able to help devastate existing Dark/Alien Sages, of which there are a few in [[Prof. Owlbrowley]] and [[Techn-Old Hyena]], which appear quite often in Zero Legends. It is important to note that these Sage enemies never come without a fair amount of support, usually from other traits that are not targeted by Gunduros, which can easily cause havoc while it tries to do anything.

With many upsides and downsides, Gunduros is a demanding unit that requires heavy strategizing to get the most out of it. But when its attack lands, expect it to devastate everything within Gunduros' standing range. It all depends on picking its battles carefully.

Lastly, Gunduros is part of the [[Royal Barrage (Combo)|Royal Barrage]] [[Cat Combo]], giving your units a Medium Attack Up (+15% Attack) for only 3 slots. This notably lets you also use another 2-slot Attack Up combo, either one of many Small Attack Up combos to get +25% attack power, or the 2-slot Medium Attack Up combo [[Land-Air Assault (Combo)|Land-Air Assault]] to get a +30% generic attack bonus, the current highest achievable with combos. This is most useful for high attack power units that don't rely on an ability that can be boosted by other combos, like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and most [[Attacks Only]] units.

